{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c55b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0d24d-9c2d-7841-a066-6ac00d915ab7"},"sequence":264,"recorded_at":1780531400000523,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"6722cf1c-e919-40c8-89ba-6768c67dec7c","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"6722cf1c-e919-40c8-89ba-6768c67dec7c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"6722cf1c-e919-40c8-89ba-6768c67dec7c"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0d24e-9833-72a0-a14d-56e68e876049"},"task_id":"01a0d24e-9833-72a0-a14d-56e68e876049","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0d24e-9833-72a0-a14d-56e68e876049","chunk":"Read text file `internal/cloneplan/doc.go`.\n1|package cloneplan\n2|\n3|// This package implements the Section 13.14.2 projection closed\n4|// schemas: Projection Plan 1.0.0 with its component records\n5|// (ProjectionItemMapping, ProjectionTargetOperation,\n6|// ExpectedTargetResource, SynthesizedProjectionEvent,\n7|// TransactionPlan, ReadBackPlan, ResumeProjectionPlan,\n8|// RollbackPlan, ContractRequirement) and Clone Projected Object\n9|// Manifest 1.0.0 with ProjectedObjectEntry. It is the second leaf\n10|// of the fidelity-projection-and-validation-contracts story: closed\n11|// shapes only. Planning semantics (strategy/profile choice,\n12|// checkpoint message authority, inactive tools/instructions, token\n13|// metadata) belong to the sibling planning leaf.\n14|//\n15|// Authority: relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.7.0, Section\n16|// 13.14.2 \"Fidelity, projection, and lineage\"\n17|// (internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md, line 10548+), the Projection\n18|// Plan 1.0.0 table, the component schemas that follow it, and the\n19|// Clone Projected Object Manifest 1.0.0 paragraph. Schema URNs come\n20|// from the Section 1 registry table (lines 168-169). Section\n21|// 13.14.4 carries no constraint on these shapes; where the plan or\n22|// manifest references sibling contracts (Migration Checkpoint,\n23|// Read-Back, Validation Report, Lineage Receipt, Bundle Manifest)\n24|// only the identity or digest field is carried.\n25|//\n26|// Every Decode entry validates a closed shape: exact members,\n27|// schema/version literals, bounded scalars, closed vocabularies,\n28|// sorted-unique order, the blob/directory nullability branches,\n29|// operation ordering with the dependency DAG, the closed plan\n30|// constants, and self-digest agreement. Every Build entry seals the\n31|// same bytes deterministically: identical inputs produce\n32|// byte-identical outputs, cross-row order is checked on the sealed\n33|// row set (never repaired), and every Build output decodes clean.\n34|// Refusals name the offending member and never admit a partial\n35|// object.\n36|//\n37|// Reuse, not fork: strict JSON framing, character string measures,\n38|// uint53/digest/UUID bounds, sorted-unique array gates, the\n39|// reverse-DNS grammar, and the SemVer grammar delegate to\n40|// internal/environ; closed extension values and the omit-self\n41|// digest construction delegate to the internal/clonebundle owner,\n42|// which also owns WorkspaceBinding validation and the nine capture\n43|// classes behind security_exclusions; Environment Tuples and\n44|// ResourceLimits decode through internal/sessadapter; the\n45|// disposition and reason vocabularies delegate to the\n46|// internal/clonefidelity sibling; canonical bytes and the SHA-256\n47|// digest come from internal/canonicaljson and internal/scalar. The\n48|// canonicaljson closed-shape registry keeps its\n49|// rejectUnsupportedImmutableObjectShape rows for these schemas\n50|// (that table's census pins every row, so replacing them would fork\n51|// ownership); this package is the validating owner and says so here\n52|// and in TRACEABILITY.md.\n53|//\n54|// Stated bounds (sibling scope or spec-silent, not waived):\n55|// canonical_event_ids equality with Canonical Session order,\n56|// item-mapping coverage (\"one for every captured/canonical item\"),\n57|// expected-resource and manifest-entry partitioning against plan\n58|// operations, synthesized insertion anchors against canonical IDs,\n59|// manifest total_bytes reconciliation (no derivation rule is\n60|// pinned), synthesized array order (array position IS the insertion\n61|// sequence), required_dispositions key closure (the request owner's\n62|// bound, mirrored exactly), and forbid_reasons admitting literal\n63|// bounded strings. This package performs no durable write: sealing\n64|// is pure bytes, so crash semantics are vacuous and determinism is\n65|// the durability proof (see TRACEABILITY.md).","final_result":true}}}
