{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c55f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0d24d-9c2d-7841-a066-6ac00d915ab7"},"sequence":266,"recorded_at":1780531400000527,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"6722cf1c-e919-40c8-89ba-6768c67dec7c","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"6722cf1c-e919-40c8-89ba-6768c67dec7c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"6722cf1c-e919-40c8-89ba-6768c67dec7c"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0d24e-9855-72e1-8a65-178b65f7feaa"},"task_id":"01a0d24e-9855-72e1-8a65-178b65f7feaa","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0d24e-9855-72e1-8a65-178b65f7feaa","chunk":"Read text file `internal/clonefidelity/doc.go`.\n1|package clonefidelity\n2|\n3|// This package implements the Section 13.14.2 fidelity contracts:\n4|// the disposition, reason, profile, and strategy vocabularies,\n5|// FidelityCounts, FidelityDispositionRecord, and Fidelity Report\n6|// 1.0.0 with its reconciliation rules. It is the first leaf of the\n7|// fidelity-projection-and-validation-contracts story.\n8|//\n9|// Authority: relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.7.0, Section\n10|// 13.14.2 \"Fidelity, projection, and lineage\"\n11|// (internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md, line 10548+). Section 13.14.4\n12|// carries no constraint on the report shape; where the report\n13|// references sibling contracts (Projection Plan, Read-Back,\n14|// Validation Report, Migration Checkpoint, Lineage Receipt) only\n15|// the identity or digest field is carried, and those contracts\n16|// belong to sibling leaves.\n17|//\n18|// Every Decode entry validates a closed shape: exact members,\n19|// bounded scalars, closed vocabularies, sorted-unique order, the\n20|// archive/target nullability branches, row ordering, aggregate\n21|// reconciliation, and self-digest agreement. BuildFidelityReport\n22|// constructs the same bytes deterministically: identical inputs\n23|// produce byte-identical outputs, counts and reason counts are\n24|// derived from the rows (never accepted), and every Build output\n25|// decodes clean. Refusals name the offending member and never admit\n26|// a partial object.\n27|//\n28|// Reuse, not fork: strict JSON framing, character string measures,\n29|// uint53/digest/UUID bounds, and sorted-unique array gates delegate\n30|// to internal/environ; the reverse-DNS grammar delegates to\n31|// environ.CheckReverseDNS; Environment Tuples decode through\n32|// sessadapter.DecodeTuple; canonical bytes and the SHA-256 digest\n33|// come from internal/canonicaljson and internal/scalar; closed\n34|// extension values, the omit-self digest construction, event kinds,\n35|// content-block types, and capture classes come from the\n36|// internal/clonebundle owner. The canonicaljson closed-shape\n37|// registry keeps its rejectUnsupportedImmutableObjectShape row for\n38|// this schema (that table's census pins every row, so replacing it\n39|// would fork ownership); this package is the validating owner and\n40|// says so here and in TRACEABILITY.md.\n41|//\n42|// Stated bounds (sibling scope, not waived): cross-artifact row\n43|// coverage (\"every Capture Manifest item and Canonical Event occurs\n44|// in exactly one non-synthesized row\") needs the manifests as\n45|// inputs and no entry in this leaf takes them; source-evidence\n46|// resolution (rows trace to captured bytes) likewise; byte_counts\n47|// values carry no row reconciliation because rows carry no byte\n48|// measure (only the exact seven-disposition key set and uint53\n49|// values are gated); the core-derived booleans admit any value\n50|// except the pinned archive rule (both target booleans false);\n51|// per-row target evidence in archive scope is admitted as shaped;\n52|// forbid_reasons admits literal bounded strings (the table row\n53|// types them as strings, not reason codes).\n54|// This package performs no durable write: sealing is pure bytes,\n55|// so crash semantics are vacuous and determinism is the durability\n56|// proof (see TRACEABILITY.md).","final_result":true}}}
