{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ca3d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0d24d-9c2d-7841-a066-6ac00d915ab7"},"sequence":889,"recorded_at":1780531400001773,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"6722cf1c-e919-40c8-89ba-6768c67dec7c","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"6722cf1c-e919-40c8-89ba-6768c67dec7c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"6722cf1c-e919-40c8-89ba-6768c67dec7c"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0d250-848d-7201-a0f3-63ab17bbaf85"},"task_id":"01a0d250-848d-7201-a0f3-63ab17bbaf85","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0d250-848d-7201-a0f3-63ab17bbaf85","chunk":"Read text file `.temp/TASK-260924-3n78rv/jmmqn-results.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-1jmmqn results: projection-plan schemas (rework rev4)\n2|\n3|Candidate: UNCOMMITTED tree in the STORY-260830-21bxa3 worktree.\n4|Scope: `internal/cloneplan` (new files only; no landed file edited,\n5|no registry edit). Change Request is `task_delta`. Base trunk\n6|`0ca3e4c` is an ancestor of the checkpoint (`git merge-base\n7|--is-ancestor 0ca3e4c HEAD` exits 0; HEAD `547ea28`): no refresh\n8|needed.\n9|\n10|This revision answers the rev3 finding\n11|(`plan-constant-second-value-uncounted`). Every rev1 finding stays\n12|closed; every rev1 production line is intact (plans.go still\n13|`sha256:c2f7eb93506291635218beb49a589d8920bf32459d2906d73c9c3c74e311f02f`,\n14|the reviewer's pinned blob). The diff is tests + harness +\n15|TRACEABILITY, plus one new test file\n16|(`constants_closed_test.go`).\n17|\n18|## What changed per the finding\n19|\n20|The rev3 finding: `TestPlanConstants` probed three invalid\n21|`materialization_intent` strings (`prepare`, `clone2`, `Clone`),\n22|so a gate widened to admit `copy` survived the submitted suite on\n23|both sides. The invalid domain of a closed constant is every other\n24|string, which is unbounded; this revision closes it BY\n25|CONSTRUCTION, exactly per the rework brief:\n26|\n27|1. Named regression (`TestPlanConstantCopyRegression`): `copy`\n28|   refuses at every closed string gate (4 nested constants +\n29|   modes + 4 schema/version literals) on both entries, 14\n30|   subtests, literal refusal tokens. Each subtest carries sibling\n31|   probes (the literal admits, the first derived neighbor\n32|   refuses), so the kill lands on the `copy-refuses` probe only.\n33|2. Generated invalid values (`TestPlanConstantGeneratedSweep`,\n34|   `TestPlanConstantDerivedValues`, `TestPlanConstantBooleans`,\n35|   `TestPlanConstantNonBooleanJSON`): per string literal at both\n36|   entries, every edit-distance-1 neighbor over\n37|   lowercase+digit+`_`, every case variant class (reusing the\n38|   census `caseVariantsOf`), a fixed-seed 200-string sample, the\n39|   `copy` probe, empty, whitespace paddings, and the 5-value\n40|   non-string JSON grid at decode; per boolean, the other boolean\n41|   both entries plus all 5 non-boolean JSON types at decode;\n42|   modes adds per-element neighbor/case sweeps, the order swap,\n43|   lengths 0..4, non-string elements, and non-array JSON. The\n44|   whole sweep runs in ~2s.\n45|3. Structural guard (`TestClosedConstantGateShape`): the gate\n46|   LIST derives mechanically (reflection over the four nested\n47|   plan input types, maps skipped by kind; build/decode functions\n48|   found by type signature; the modes checker found by call\n49|   shape), cross-checked both directions against the spec oracle\n50|   (SPEC.v0.7.0.md:10703-10718, 10654, 168-169). Each gate must\n51|   be one equality against the oracle literal; the\n52|   comparison-literal set per file must equal the oracle set\n53|   exactly; no switch, no prefix/fold/contains/normalize call.\n54|   Control plants: the reviewer's build-side copy widening\n55|   reddens it (exit 1), a two-case switch reddens it (exit 1),\n56|   and a bonus decode-side copy widening reddens it (exit 1);\n57|   pristine passes (exit 0). Production restored byte-identical\n58|   after each plant (sha re-verified).\n59|4. Mutants: 13 copy-admitting narrowings (`N-copy-*`, one per\n60|   string gate per side plus the shared modes gate and the 4\n61|   decode-only schema/version literals) killed by the named\n62|   copy-regression subtests ALONE, and 7 null-admitting decode\n63|   narrowings (`N-null-*`, one per closed boolean gate) killed by\n64|   the named non-boolean subtests ALONE. Battery is now 145 rows:\n65|   143 narrowing + 1 marked arm-delete + 1 neutral control\n66|   SURVIVED.\n67|\n68|## AC coverage, measured: 18 of 18 leaf-schema rows driven\n69|\n70|Denominator: the 18 leaf-schema rows (planning semantics excluded\n71|per the orchestrator split). Each row names its production call\n72|site; every refusal below is literal-pinned and every gate carries\n73|a killed narrowing (matrix names them). Rows 8-11 are now carried\n74|by the construction above; all other rows unchanged from rev2.\n75|\n76|| # | Row | Call site | Test |\n77||---|---|---|---|\n78|| 1 | Plan 36-member set + schema/version literals | D | Derived census + UnknownMissing + Miscased(6 classes) + WrongTypes + Duplicated(every member) + NoLiteralList + SchemaLiterals + CopyRegression + DerivedValues + GeneratedSweep + GateShape |\n79|| 2 | `projection_plan_id` omit-self identity | B, D | TestPlanIdentityIndependent |\n80|| 3 | Mapping shape + disposition/reason vocabs | B, D | Census + ExpectedDisposition/MappingReason oracles |\n81|| 4 | Operation shape + sequence order | B, D | Census + DAGRefusalLiterals |\n82|| 5 | Dependency DAG vs oracle | B, D (shared gate) | WholeDomainCensus + ValidFive + Locality + SingleEdge + RefusalLiterals |\n83|| 6 | Resource branch-exact nullability | B, D (shared gate) | ResourceNullabilityGrid (12/12 full) + BranchLiterals |\n84|| 7 | Synth event shape + purposes | B, D | Census + SynthesizedPurposeOracle |\n85|| 8-11 | Transaction/ReadBack/Resume/Rollback constants | B, D | TestPlanConstants +