lector that finds\\n# nothing fails closed instead of passing on an empty result set. No job\\n# declares an `if:` condition, so no job can skip quietly; gates-verdict\\n# additionally refuses any skipped, failed, or cancelled dependency.\\n#\\n# GOOS=windows work is compile-and-vet only. A green windows-compile-only job\\n# proves the tree type-checks for Windows; it never implies executed\\n# behaviour. Coverage is reported as numbers, not enforced as a floor.\\njobs:\\n  contract-preservation:\\n    name: Contract preservation (v0.5.0 current, v0.4.3 historical)\\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\\n    timeout-minutes: 10\\n    steps:\\n      - name: Check out repository\\n        uses: actions/checkout@v7\\n\\n      - name: Set up Go\\n        uses: actions/setup-go@v7\\n        with:\\n          go-version-file: go.mod\\n\\n      - name: Verify specification-to-code ownership\\n        run: go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck\\n\\n      # The diff proves the committed catalog matches generator output, but\\n      # `go generate` runs nothing when its directive is disarmed: rewriting\\n      # `//go:generate` as `// go:generate` preserves the token while turning\\n      # the directive into a plain comment, so generation is skipped and the\\n      # diff stays clean. The anchored check refuses that token-preserving\\n      # rewrite; only the exact directive form counts. A new directive\\n      # without a pin update reddens here (and in\\n      # TestGenerateDirectiveStaysRecognizedForm) instead of going unchecked.\\n      - name: Verify generated catalog is current\\n        run: |\\n          test \\\"$(grep -c '^//go:generate' internal/catalog/catalog.go)\\\" -eq 1\\n          go generate ./internal/catalog\\n          git diff --exit-code -- internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go\\n\\n      # The release roots are derived from internal/specpin and\\n      # internal/catalog inside the gate, never retyped here. Each -- PASS\\n      # guard below must match: a selector that runs nothing fails here\\n      # instead of passing silently.\\n      - name: Run pinned contract-version gates\\n        run: |\\n          set +e\\n          go test ./internal/cigate -run 'TestVerifyContractPreservationLive|TestPinnedReleasesAgreeAcrossAuthorities|TestDerivedSetsAreComplete|TestCheckAgreementAdmitsIdenticalSets|TestCheckAgreementRefusals|TestCheckReleaseRootsRefusesDrift' -count=1 -v > cigate-contracts.log 2>&1\\n          code=$?\\n===\\n260829_024701_epic-260829-dz9yvx.md\\n260830_020530_project.md\\n260830_020537_epic-260830-1ewjla.md\\n260830_020537_epic-260830-1uwj54.md\\n260830_020537_epic-260830-27bix9.md\\n260830_020537_epic-260830-391tge.md\\n260830_020537_epic-260830-3v9jlg.md\\n260830_020538_task-260830-55kcni.md\\n260830_021436_epic-260830-37rgqn.md\\n===\\nadoption-v0.6.0.md\\nadoption-v0.7.0.md\\ncmd\\nownership.v0.5.0.json\\nownership.v0.6.0.json\\nownership.v0.7.0.json\\nreadme_figures_pin_test.go\\nregistry_rederivation_test.go\\ntraceability_test.go\\ntraceability.go\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 3843,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 961,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
